has only 10 times more Fintech companies&nbsp;
despite having 59 times more inhabitants!
 &nbsp;

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:58.500
But... We are not only talking about the&nbsp;
digital world. What if I told you that one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:03.000
of the sectors that has been growing the most&nbsp;
lately in this micro-country is, precisely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:07.620
manufacturing? What if I told you that this&nbsp;
sector is the top priority of the 2030 plan?
 &nbsp;

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:12.300
Yes, despite the fact that Singapore is a very&nbsp;
small place, the manufacturing sector accounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:17.580
for 22% of its GDP. To give you an idea, in&nbsp;
Spain, France and the United Kingdom this sector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:23.040
accounts for 13%, 10% and 9% respectively.
 
In fact, one out of every eight jobs in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.860
Singapore is in manufacturing.
 
As you can see, it's not all big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:29.940
skyscrapers of banks and insurance companies.&nbsp;
There is a lot more to Singapore. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.480
if you are thinking of shoe or toy factories,&nbsp;
you can put that out of your mind.
 &nbsp;

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:42.600
Singapore specializes in highly advanced, high&nbsp;
value-added manufacturing, such as electronics.
 &nbsp;

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:45.720
This includes semiconductors,&nbsp;
precision engineering, chemicals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:49.020
and also the production of components&nbsp;
for the aerospace industry. In total,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:52.800
advanced industries account for&nbsp;
around 80% of all production.
 &nbsp;

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.420
Just as Switzerland has succeeded in creating&nbsp;
highly specialized and sophisticated industries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:04.080
such as the biomedical industry,&nbsp;
Singapore is doing exactly the same.
 &nbsp;

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.680
But now the government intends to go much&nbsp;
further, and has created a plan in which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:12.240
robotics and artificial intelligence play a key&nbsp;
role. The goal is to eventually reduce local,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:21.540
low value-added jobs to an absolute minimum.
 
The idea is not only that low value-added jobs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:26.040
will be reduced in number, but that those who&nbsp;
work them will commute daily from the border&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.320
Malaysian state of Johor.
 
And the truth is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:31.080
they are on the right track.
 
To give you an idea, in the five-year period&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:37.440
2017-2021, manufacturing labor productivity&nbsp;
grew by an average of 11.9% per year.
 &nbsp;

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:44.220
Now, why do Singaporeans believe that they&nbsp;
